<p><strong>Introduction:</strong></p>
<p>This analysis uses a wine review dataset obtained from Kaggle, which contains detailed reviews of wines from various countries, provinces, and grape varieties around the world. After cleaning the data, the dataset includes over 12,000 observations, each with information on the wine’s origin, grape variety, price, and rating.</p>
<p>How does the country/providence of origin, variety of grape, and price affect the overall rating of the wine?</p>
<p>Link to data set: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/zynicide/wine-reviews</p>
<p><strong>The Variables:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><p>country: Country of origin</p></li>
<li><p>providence: Providence of origin</p></li>
<li><p>points: Number of points WineEnthusiast rated the wine on a scale of 1-100</p></li>
<li><p>price: The cost for a bottle of the wine</p></li>
<li><p>variety: Grape type</p></li>
</ul>
