<p>Interpretation:</p>
<p>This scatterplot shows a generally positive relationship between average price and average rating across grape varieties, though the relationship is modest rather than strong. Higher-priced varieties such as Pinot Noir and Syrah tend to have higher average ratings, clustering near the top of the graph. In contrast, lower-priced varieties like Rosé and Merlot sit toward the lower end of the rating scale, though the differences in average points are relatively small overall.</p>
