<p>Interpretation:</p>
<p>This boxplot compares the distribution of wine ratings across countries with more than 400 reviewed wines, with color indicating each country’s average price binned into $5 increments. While there is some variation in median ratings, most countries cluster between roughly 86 and 90 points, suggesting that overall quality is relatively consistent among countries. Countries with higher average prices do not always have higher average ratings, indicating that price alone does not guarantee more points.</p>
